<!-- ROAD TESTS -->
<div class="panel" id="panel-road">
<div class="wrap">
  <div class="eyebrow" style="color:var(--water)">Road Test Analysis — Phase 21 Estimates</div>
  <h2 class="section-title">Speed · Range · Torque — CVT Hydrostatic · Rear 2WD · 75mm Bore · 250mm Stroke</h2>
  <p class="section-lead">CVT hydrostatic replaces the 4-speed manual. Speed estimates change: CVT gives continuous ratio variation from stall to max RPM. No discrete gear steps. Torque delivery is smoother — CVT multiplies torque at low speed and steps back at cruise. Chevy Impala base ~1,650 kg. Phase 21 estimated ~1,980 kg (CVT ~40 kg lighter than 4-speed + worm gearbox combo). Rear 2WD only in Phase 21.</p>

  <div class="tbl">
  <table>
  <thead><tr><th>CVT State</th><th>Ratio (variable)</th><th>Engine RPM</th><th>Est. Wheel RPM</th><th>Est. Speed</th><th>Est. Wheel Torque</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  <tr><td style="color:var(--cvt)">Full stall torque</td><td>Max ratio (CVT low)</td><td>200 RPM</td><td>~6 RPM</td><td>~3 MPH</td><td>~50,000+ Nm est.</td></tr>
  <tr><td style="color:var(--cvt)">Low speed</td><td>High ratio</td><td>200 RPM</td><td>~12 RPM</td><td>~7 MPH</td><td>~25,000 Nm est.</td></tr>
  <tr><td style="color:var(--cvt)">Mid speed</td><td>Mid ratio</td><td>200 RPM</td><td>~25 RPM</td><td>~14 MPH</td><td>~12,000 Nm est.</td></tr>
  <tr><td style="color:var(--cvt)">Cruise</td><td>Low ratio (CVT high)</td><td>200 RPM</td><td>~45 RPM</td><td>~26 MPH</td><td>~6,700 Nm est.</td></tr>
  <tr><td style="color:var(--cvt)">Top (EWI boost)</td><td>Min ratio</td><td>200 RPM</td><td>~55 RPM</td><td>~31 MPH</td><td>~5,500 Nm est.</td></tr>
  <tr><td style="color:var(--safe)">Reverse</td><td>CVT reverse mode</td><td>200 RPM</td><td>~8 RPM</td><td>~5 MPH</td><td>~37,500 Nm est.</td></tr>
  </tbody>
  </table>
  </div>

  <div class="new-box">
    <h4>▶ PHASE 21 CVT ADVANTAGES OVER PHASE 20 4-SPEED</h4>
    <ul>
      <li>No torque dip on shift — 4-speed had a dead moment at every gear change, CVT is continuous</li>
      <li>Stall torque is higher — CVT can multiply torque more aggressively at very low speed than a fixed 1st gear could</li>
      <li>No clutch needed — hydrostatic CVT has built-in fluid coupling, engagement is smooth from zero</li>
      <li>Simpler drivetrain — CVT replaces gearbox + worm spine drive path + 4WD transfer case, fewer failure points</li>
      <li>Reverse is inherent — CVT hydrostatic reverses by pump direction, no reverse gear needed</li>
      <li>Range unchanged — water system, boiler, condenser all Phase 20 spec, range still near-unlimited with condenser</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="warn-box">
    <h4>⚠ Road Test Notes — Phase 21</h4>
    <ul>
      <li>Top speed similar to Phase 20 at ~31 MPH — engine ceiling at 200 RPM is the limiting factor in both phases</li>
      <li>Rear 2WD instead of 4WD — traction on loose/wet surfaces reduced vs Phase 20. Front axle is free-rolling only</li>
      <li>CVT hydrostatic needs high-pressure hydraulic fluid — maintain fluid level and filter schedule carefully</li>
      <li>Three locked diffs all driving one shaft: if any one shaft seizes, it locks the driveshaft — inspect diffs at each service</li>
      <li>CVT efficiency: hydrostatic CVTs have ~85% efficiency vs ~95% for a locked gear — small power loss at cruise acceptable given steam torque surplus</li>
      <li>EWI calibration: unchanged from Phase 20 — PID tuning needed before road use</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="metrics">
    <div class="metric"><div class="val" style="color:var(--pass)">~31</div><div class="lbl">Max MPH Est.</div></div>
    <div class="metric"><div class="val" style="color:var(--elec)">~50k+</div><div class="lbl">Nm Stall Torque Est.</div></div>
    <div class="metric"><div class="val" style="color:var(--new)">~0</div><div class="lbl">Net Water Use (condenser)</div></div>
    <div class="metric"><div class="val" style="color:var(--water)">74s</div><div class="lbl">Cold Start</div></div>
    <div class="metric"><div class="val" style="color:var(--new)">∞</div><div class="lbl">Range w/ Condenser</div></div>
    <div class="metric"><div class="val" style="color:var(--muted)">TBD</div><div class="lbl">Rolling Road Test</div></div>
  </div>
</div>
</div>

