  <div class="new-box">
    <h4>▶ PHASE 21 SAFETY ADDITIONS</h4>
    <ul>
      <li>CVT overheat monitoring: hydrostatic fluid at 115°C triggers warning, throttle auto-reduce prevents fluid breakdown</li>
      <li>Diff alignment vibration sensor: if any of the three diffs develops a misalignment, driveshaft vibration changes — sensor flags this before catastrophic failure</li>
      <li>Oil temp monitoring at all three diff locations: not just one sensor as in Phase 20 worm — each locked diff coupling point gets its own thermocouple</li>
      <li>Rear 2WD means no front axle shaft failure mode — Phase 20 4WD had front prop and transfer case as additional failure points</li>
      <li>CVT hydraulic reverse eliminates need for reverse gear engagement — reduces drivetrain stress on direction change</li>
    </ul>
