  <div class="warn-box">
    <h4>⚠ Phase 21 Cost Notes</h4>
    <ul>
      <li>Worm spine + 4-speed gearbox + 4WD transfer case removed — saves ~$5,500 combined</li>
      <li>Three locked diffs on cylinder shafts + amber driveshaft + CVT add ~$5,500 — roughly cost-neutral overall</li>
      <li>Phase 21 total estimate ~$35–39K vs Phase 20 ~$37–41K — slightly cheaper due to simpler drivetrain</li>
      <li>CVT hydrostatic must be sized to handle combined steam torque — do not underspec the unit. Budget for a heavy-duty agricultural or industrial CVT if automotive units are insufficient torque rating.</li>
      <li>Custom locked diffs for 60mm cylinder shafts: no off-the-shelf unit. Budget machining time or find an industrial dog clutch equivalent that can be adapted.</li>
      <li>Front axle no longer driven — front CV joints, front diff, and front prop all removed, saving ~$1,800 and ~38 kg vs Phase 20</li>
    </ul>
